The plugin hooks Hermes's own request middleware and hands user-role text to
Presidio, with a separately provisioned spaCy model reading names, places and
organizations. This rewrite keeps the shape and drops the Python: the cell
advises the fold that projects the event log onto provider-shaped messages,
redacts the user-role text of a copy, and hands the fold's clean flag back.
The detectors are local string rules -- an address, a phone number written
with a plus or separators, a checksum-valid card number, an IBAN whose
remainder checks, a dotted IPv4 address -- and the same union-of-overlaps
mask names the placeholder, structured kinds first. What was left out: the
spaCy model, so a person or a place is masked only when the operator lists
the word in `terms`, and a phone is read by its written shape rather than by
libphonenumber. The Italian model, the score threshold, the language
setting and the fail-open warning class wording went with them; the
fail-open policy itself, the copy-not-in-place rewrite, the user-role-only
whitelist and the no-recovery-map masking are kept.